  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1117 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nThe ridge continues to build over the southeast Wednesday night \ninto Friday. This should really lower shower/storm chances to \nbetween 10 and 30 percent in the afternoon. Highs will likely \nrise into the mid 90s at least by Friday (maybe Thursday). Based \non forecast 925 mb temperatures, conditions could be hotter, \nmaybe some upper 90s in a few locations. This will likely amplify \na heat wave that will continue into the weekend. Highs in guidance\nlook a bit low based on forecast 925 mb temperatures. \n\nOn Friday, most models build the center of the upper ridge over\nArkansas and Mississippi. This further strengthens the upper ridge\nover the area. This should push highs into the 95 to 100 degree \nrange. The heat wave will likely peak over the upcoming weekend. \nWith some 925 mb temperatures forecast, we could climb over the \ncentury mark during that period. Extreme heat products may be \nneeded over the weekend.",
